# Line endings are normalised to LF everywhere: in the repository and in the
# working copy. Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true warns
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on every commit, and a contributor on Linux
# produces blobs that differ from a Windows one for no semantic reason.
#
# LF in the working copy is deliberate rather than a side effect: it keeps the
# checked-out bytes identical to the stored bytes, so byte-for-byte comparisons
# (tier 0 compares installed skill bodies against the repository) cannot fail
# because of a platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Embeds NUL bytes on purpose, to prove the SessionStart hook survives a ledger
# it cannot parse. Git would guess "binary" and leave it alone in most cases,
# but say so explicitly — normalising this file would corrupt the exact bytes
# it exists to exercise.
tests/tier2-hook.test.js -text
